# Food Ordering System - Environment Configuration Example

## Database Configuration
DB_HOST=localhost
DB_USER=root
DB_PASSWORD=
DB_NAME=food_ordering_system

## Site Configuration
SITE_URL=http://localhost/FoodSystem/
SITE_NAME=Food Ordering System
ADMIN_EMAIL=admin@foodsystem.com

## Email Configuration (Optional - for future implementation)
MAIL_DRIVER=smtp
MAIL_HOST=smtp.mailtrap.io
MAIL_PORT=2525
MAIL_USERNAME=
MAIL_PASSWORD=
MAIL_ENCRYPTION=tls
MAIL_FROM_ADDRESS=noreply@foodsystem.com
MAIL_FROM_NAME="Food Ordering System"

## Payment Gateway Configuration (Optional)
STRIPE_PUBLIC_KEY=
STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=

PAYPAL_CLIENT_ID=
PAYPAL_CLIENT_SECRET=

## Session Configuration
SESSION_TIMEOUT=1800
SESSION_SECURE=false
SESSION_HTTPONLY=true
SESSION_SAMESITE=Lax

## Security Configuration
ENCRYPTION_KEY=
CSRF_TOKEN_ENABLED=true
DEBUG_MODE=false

## File Upload Configuration
MAX_UPLOAD_SIZE=5242880
ALLOWED_FILE_TYPES=jpg,jpeg,png,gif
UPLOAD_PATH=/uploads/

## Application Configuration
APP_ENV=production
APP_DEBUG=false
LOG_LEVEL=error
PAGINATION_LIMIT=20

## SMS Configuration (Optional - for future implementation)
SMS_DRIVER=twilio
TWILIO_SID=
TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=
TWILIO_PHONE=

## API Configuration (Optional - for future implementation)
API_RATE_LIMIT=100
API_TIMEOUT=30
API_VERSION=v1

## Social Media Configuration (Optional)
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
FACEBOOK_APP_ID=
FACEBOOK_APP_SECRET=

---

## PRODUCTION NOTES

### Before Deploying:

1. Change database password
2. Use strong CSRF token
3. Enable HTTPS (SESSION_SECURE=true)
4. Set APP_ENV=production
5. Set APP_DEBUG=false
6. Configure email service
7. Set up backups
8. Enable logging
9. Configure SSL certificates
10. Update firewall rules

### Local Development:
```
DB_HOST=localhost
DB_USER=root
DB_PASSWORD=
APP_ENV=development
APP_DEBUG=true
SESSION_SECURE=false
```

### Production Setup:
```
DB_HOST=production-db-server
DB_USER=prod_user
DB_PASSWORD=strong_password_here
APP_ENV=production
APP_DEBUG=false
SESSION_SECURE=true
```

### Security Checklist:
- [ ] Database passwords changed
- [ ] Admin password changed
- [ ] API keys configured
- [ ] Email service configured
- [ ] SSL/HTTPS enabled
- [ ] Backups configured
- [ ] Error logging enabled
- [ ] Security headers set
- [ ] Firewall configured
- [ ] Regular updates scheduled

---

## Notes for Customization

Replace the following values based on your setup:
- DB_HOST: Your database server
- DB_USER: Database username
- DB_PASSWORD: Database password (leave empty for localhost)
- SITE_URL: Your application URL
- MAIL_* settings: Your email service credentials
- STRIPE_* or PAYPAL_*: Payment gateway credentials
- TWILIO_*: SMS service credentials
- SOCIAL_*: Social login credentials

All passwords and sensitive data should be:
- Changed before production deployment
- Stored securely
- Never committed to version control
- Updated regularly
- Protected with proper file permissions

---

**Important**: Keep this file secure and never expose sensitive information!
